- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/camera.html
- Summary (EN): Creates a default perspective camera offset back from the layer centre according to Focal Length and Aperture. Its settings override the default_camera context option set by the Default Canvas. Available since version 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud camera crée une caméra perspective par défaut, reculée du centre de la couche selon la focale et l'ouverture, et ses réglages remplacent la caméra par défaut du Default Canvas.

- Inputs meaning: ["camera_ref (optional): camera layer; Set Parameters from Input populates the parameters from it"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Set Parameters from Input", "meaning": "Autofills the parameters from the connected camera_ref"}, {"name": "Transform", "meaning": "Translate, Rotate, Transform Order, Pivot Translate, Pivot Rotate"}, {"name": "Look At", "meaning": "Look At Position, Up Vector Method (Y Axis, X Axis, Custom), Twist"}, {"name": "View", "meaning": "Resolution, Projection, Focal Length, Aperture, Ortho Width, Near and Far Clipping, Screen Window, Crop, Imaging Distance, Guide Scale"}, {"name": "Sampling", "meaning": "Shutter Open and Close, Focus Distance, F-Stop"}, {"name": "Metadata", "meaning": "Key/value entries of the metadata dictionary"}]

- Caveats: ["Only the ratio of Focal Length to Aperture sets the camera offset", "Imaging Distance is measured in Houdini units", "Guide Scale applies only when the layer is shown as metadata"]

